\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The shepherds had an angel,
\par The wise men had a star;
\par But what have I, a little child,
\par To guide me home from far,
\par Where glad stars sing together,
\par And singing angels are?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Lord Jesus is my guardian,
\par So I can nothing lack:
\par The lambs lie in His bosom,
\par Along life's dangerous track;
\par The wilful lambs that go astray
\par He, bleeding, fetches back.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Those shepherds through the lonely night
\par Sat watching by their sheep,
\par Until they saw the heavenly host
\par Who neither tire nor sleep,
\par All singing Glory, glory
\par In festival they keep.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Christ watches me, His little lamb,
\par Cares for me day and night,
\par That I may be his own in heaven:
\par So agels clad in white,
\par Shall sing their Glory, glory\tab 
\par For my sake in the height.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Lord, bring me nearer day by day,
\par Till I my voice unite,
\par And sing my Glory, glory
\par With angels clad in white,
\par All Glory, glory given to Thee
\par Through all the heavenly height.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

